# SPA routes, enumerated on purpose.
#
# A catch-all `/*  /index.html  200` used to sit at the bottom of this file,
# which meant every URL on the domain answered 200 with the app shell — a soft
# 404. Agents probing for `/api`, `/docs` or `/.well-known/…` concluded that
# every path existed, and a crawler could index unlimited duplicates of the
# same shell.
#
# Listing the real routes lets everything else fall through to `404.html`,
# which Netlify serves with a genuine 404 status. `/blog/:slug` still resolves
# here; whether that *slug* exists is a database question, answered in
# netlify/edge-functions/blog-meta.ts.
#
# Adding a client route in `src/main.tsx` or `src/blog/BlogApp.tsx` means adding
# it here *and* in netlify/edge-functions/_routes.ts. `tests/routes.test.ts`
# fails when the three drift.
/                 /index.html   200
/blog             /index.html   200
/blog/*           /index.html   200
/admin            /index.html   200
/admin/*          /index.html   200

# /developers is a standalone document, not a client route — it points at its
# own file rather than the app shell.
#
# A flat `developers.html`, not `developers/index.html`: Netlify 301s a request
# for `/developers` to `/developers/` when a directory of that name exists, and
# a canonical URL that costs an extra round trip is a canonical URL agents will
# disagree with. With no directory there is nothing to redirect to, and this
# rewrite serves the file at the canonical path with a 200.
/developers       /developers.html         200

# Public content API. The payloads are static JSON generated from
# `src/data/api.ts` (see tests/api-payloads.test.ts, which writes them), so
# these endpoints cost a file read and no compute. Extensionless paths are the
# ones documented in /openapi.json, hence the rewrites.
#
# /api/v1/posts is absent on purpose: it is served live from Firestore by
# netlify/edge-functions/api.ts, which also turns every unmatched /api/ path
# into an RFC 9457 problem+json instead of the HTML 404 page.
/api/v1           /api/v1/index.json       200
/api/v1/profile   /api/v1/profile.json     200
/api/v1/projects  /api/v1/projects.json    200
/api/v1/experience  /api/v1/experience.json  200
/api/v1/stack     /api/v1/stack.json       200
